{"p4": {"friction": "Claim 2's object names a result (\"Cleyton–Ivanov theorem\") rather than stating it. The rubric flags this form issue only as a conjectures near-miss, not for proves. Several subjects are a remark plus an equation label (\"Remark 13 (4.54)\"), and the rubric doesn't say whether an equation label belongs in the subject.", "doubt": "Claim 12: (3.8) is cited in Remark 5 as \"the identity (3.8)\" but its text is missing, so the compound locator is hard to check. Claim 17: the abstract describes Corollary 1's content without naming it.", "missing_context": "The paper text is truncated and excerpted: equations (3.8), (4.28)–(4.37) and the §4–§6 body text are absent.", "proposed_change": "In the proves section, state that the object must be the statement itself, not the name of a theorem (e.g. \"X theorem\"), matching the conjectures form near-miss.", "process_observation": "The grader input was cut off mid-formula at line 142 before the claims list. The excerpt holds only definition, proposition, remark and corollary blocks, so text that sits between them, such as proof bodies, is missing."}}
